- src/virtualenv/util/subprocess/__init__.py:10 — generic `run_cmd` helper; all callers pass list-form commands built from interpreter paths / fixed flags, no shell=True, no user-controlled string concatenation. FALSE POSITIVE.
- src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/acquire.py:74 — `Popen` of `sys.executable -m pip download` with a package spec passed as a distinct argv element (no shell). FALSE POSITIVE.
- src/virtualenv/discovery/cached_py_info.py:130 — `Popen` of a discovered interpreter with the bundled `py_info.py` script and generated cookies; argv list, no shell. FALSE POSITIVE.
- src/virtualenv/create/via_global_ref/builtin/cpython/mac_os.py:124 — `install_name_tool -change` with paths from the created environment, argv list. FALSE POSITIVE.
- src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/periodic_update.py:211 — background updater launched with `sys.executable -c` and `{!r}`-formatted literals (properly quoted, not shell-interpolated). FALSE POSITIVE.
- src/virtualenv/seed/embed/pip_invoke.py:29 — seeding via `Popen(cmd, env=env)` with a list command built from fixed pip flags and wheel paths. FALSE POSITIVE.
- src/virtualenv/seed/embed/via_app_data/pip_install/symlink.py:16 — `python -m compileall <image_dir>`, list argv, no shell. FALSE POSITIVE.
- tasks/upgrade_wheels.py:23 and tasks/upgrade_wheels.py:125 — developer build scripts (constantly-run tooling), not part of the shipped runtime library; arguments are controlled by maintainers. FALSE POSITIVE (build/task scripts, not exploitable by an attacker).
- tasks/make_zipapp.py:241 — same developer build script category; argv list. FALSE POSITIVE.
- tasks/release.py:57 — release automation script executed by maintainers only. FALSE POSITIVE.

No genuine shell-injection (CWE-78) or path-traversal (CWE-22) vectors were confirmed: all subprocess invocations use sequence arguments without shell=True and with fixed/validated paths, and the zipapp extraction target name is normalised to `dest.name` inside a validated destination folder.
