2026-11-22 15:55:21 - Agent_20261122155316 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed the single CodeQL result for py/virtualenv/insecure-network in src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/periodic_update.py. Investigated the whole PyPI metadata retrieval path (release_date_for_wheel_path -> _pypi_get_distribution_info_cached -> _pypi_get_distribution_info -> _request_context) plus downstream use of the fetched data in _run_do_update (release dates drive GRACE_PERIOD_MINOR decisions about which latest wheel virtualenv seeds/installs).

Confirmed two TP instances:
1. L353 `with urlopen(url, context=context) as file_handler:` — first attempt uses default (verified) context, but on any URLError the loop falls through to an unverified TLS context, so a network attacker who can force that error gets MITM'd PyPI metadata with no integrity check.
2. L336 `yield ssl._create_unverified_context()` in the _request_context fallback generator — cert validation, hostname verification and CA pinning are all disabled (explicitly noqa: S323), enabling a MITM to forge `upload_time` values and thereby manipulate virtualenv's version-age gating (a supply-chain relevant integrity issue, CWE-295/CWE-319).

No additional distinct network-sink issues were found: wheel download itself is delegated to `pip download` (src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/acquire.py:53), which uses its own verified TLS / index validation, so that path is not part of this vulnerability.
