2026-11-22 15:55:48 - Agent_20261122155316 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed the single CodeQL result for py/virtualenv/unverified-ssl at src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/periodic_update.py:336. The `_request_context()` generator yields None first (default verified TLS), then falls back to `ssl._create_unverified_context()`, which is passed as `context=` to `urlopen()` for the PyPI JSON API request in `_pypi_get_distribution_info()`. Confirmed as a true positive (low severity, CWE-295): the fallback silently disables certificate verification, so on a MITM/blocked-verification network path the attacker can supply forged release metadata (upload_time / release ordering) that influences virtualenv's automatic wheel update decisions — and more importantly normalizes an insecure TLS posture. Impact is bounded because only public, non-sensitive PyPI metadata is fetched, the failure path requires the verified request to fail first, and CodeQL reported no derived dataflow; the finding was submitted as a low-severity true positive. No additional distinct vulnerable locations exist for this rule in the package (grep confirmed only one `_create_unverified_context` occurrence and one `urlopen` sink, with no other SSL context creation in src/).
